  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a member, I want Réglages › « Style des messages » to **show what Moderne and Classique change**: a small live preview of two messages under the picker. I cannot tell the difference from the names alone; it is not a font change. (Operator feedback, 2026-11-17.)\n\n### What the two styles change (dev-swift)\n\n`<body class=\"style-modern|style-classic\">` comes from `TopicHTMLBuilder.swift:90`. The rules are in `App/SwiftHFR/Reader/Resources/reader.css`:\n\n| | Moderne (default) | Classique |\n|---|---|---|\n| Message header band | barely tinted: 3 % accent (`:117`) | clearly tinted: 15 % accent (`:118`), also on my own messages (`:192`) |\n| Text position | indented under the avatar (`--indent`, `:127`, `:195`) | starts at the left margin; 8 px space above the text (`:120`) |\n| Alternating messages | none | even messages get their own header band over the background (`:200-204`) |\n| Whitelisted author | light love tint and border (`:196`, `:206`) | full love colour on header and text (`:197`, `:207`) |\n\nThe font, size and spacing settings are unchanged; they come from the other settings. Legacy has the same picker (`AppSettingsView.swift:471-472` @ 87fe0d1c, `theme_style`, default 1 = modern).\n\n### Scope\n\n1. Under the picker (`App/SwiftHFR/Settings/SettingsView.swift:140`), add a **non-interactive preview** of two short sample messages, one odd and one even, with neutral sample pseudos and no real member. Render it with the **real reader pipeline** (`TopicHTMLBuilder` plus `reader.css`, current theme, density and text size), so it can never drift from the reader. It updates live when the choice changes.\n2. Add one short sentence under the preview: « Moderne : texte aligné sous l'avatar, en-têtes discrets. Classique : en-têtes colorés et alternés, texte à la marge. » Adjust the wording to the verified table.\n3. Keep it light: one small web view, created when the settings screen appears. No network: sample content only, with no image or with a bundled placeholder avatar.\n4. Accessibility: the preview is hidden from VoiceOver; the sentence carries the meaning.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- A test that the preview's HTML carries the selected `style-*` class and the sample messages, and no network URL.\n- A test of the sentence per style.\n- Tests fail without the change.\n\n### Device check (for the #893 general review)\n\nSwitching the style changes the preview at once, in light and dark.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
